3. Relabellings theta_eps = (conj^e1, conj^e2), eps in {+1,-1}^2 (Thm 3)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
(a) the image of g, and of su+su, on L does not depend on eps:
  (2,2): d rho_eps(g) = l (dim 7, contains i 1_L) and d rho_eps(su+su) = l_0 (dim 6) for all four eps
  (2,3): d rho_eps(g) = l (dim 12, contains i 1_L) and d rho_eps(su+su) = l_0 (dim 11) for all four eps
  (3,3): d rho_eps(g) = l (dim 17, contains i 1_L) and d rho_eps(su+su) = l_0 (dim 16) for all four eps
(b) theta_eps maps the trace functional tr1 + tr2 to e1 tr1 + e2 tr2 (tr conj(X) = -tr X on u(d)):
  checked on bases of u(2), u(3); so theta_eps^{-1}(h_W) = h_W iff e1 = e2
(c) the Letter's h_W = s(u(d1)+u(d2)) under the link action rho_eps; its centre Q = i(d2 1, -d1 1):
   eps     | type  | Q on L (/i) | i 1_L in d rho_eps(h_W)? | acting
   (1, 1)  | (2,2) |           0 |                    False | False
   (1, 1)  | (2,3) |           1 |                     True | True
   (1, 1)  | (3,3) |           0 |                    False | False
   (-1, -1)| (2,2) |           0 |                    False | False
   (-1, -1)| (2,3) |          -1 |                     True | True
   (-1, -1)| (3,3) |           0 |                    False | False
   (1, -1) | (2,2) |           4 |                     True | True
   (1, -1) | (2,3) |           5 |                     True | True
   (1, -1) | (3,3) |           6 |                     True | True
   (-1, 1) | (2,2) |          -4 |                     True | True
   (-1, 1) | (2,3) |          -5 |                     True | True
   (-1, 1) | (3,3) |          -6 |                     True | True
  the acting predicate depends on eps only through e1 e2: e1 e2 = +1 gives reading A (acting iff d1 != d2),
  e1 e2 = -1 gives reading A* (acting at every type).  (asserted)
(d) the automorphism U -> conj(U):
  SU(2): sigma_y conj(U) sigma_y = U for U = [[a,-conj b],[b,conj a]] (inner);
  U(2):  sigma_y conj(e^{i phi} U) sigma_y = e^{-2 i phi} (e^{i phi} U): the central phase is inverted (not inner)
  SU(3): U = diag(i, i, -1) has det 1, tr U = -1+2i, tr conj(U) = -1-2i; inner automorphisms keep the trace,
         so conj is outer on SU(3).  By (a) it does not change the image of su+su on L; it relabels 3 <-> 3bar.
(e) transposition at both ends (the covariant exchange E' = E o T of CT-G11 transposes every slot):
  (X1(x)1+1(x)X2)^T = -(conj X1 (x) 1 + 1 (x) conj X2) on every basis element at (2,2),(2,3),(3,3):
  it is the diagonal relabelling eps = (-1,-1), e1 e2 = +1, which keeps the selection and sends Y to -Y.

