  (2,3): <su+su, m_0> has dim 12 = d1^2+d2^2-1 and lies in ker(tr1+tr2) = s(u(d1)+u(d2)); <su+su, stab> has dim 13 (= g)
  (3,3): <su+su, m_0> has dim 17 = d1^2+d2^2-1 and lies in ker(tr1+tr2) = s(u(d1)+u(d2)); <su+su, stab> has dim 17 (= s(u+u))
  (2,4): <su+su, m_0> has dim 19 = d1^2+d2^2-1 and lies in ker(tr1+tr2) = s(u(d1)+u(d2)); <su+su, stab> has dim 20 (= g)
  (3,4): <su+su, m_0> has dim 24 = d1^2+d2^2-1 and lies in ker(tr1+tr2) = s(u(d1)+u(d2)); <su+su, stab> has dim 25 (= g)
(c) matching closure over the invariant hyperplanes h_[alpha:beta] = {alpha tr X1 + beta tr X2 = 0}:
